      "id": "summary",
      "proposition": {
        "predicate": "summary",
        "object": "<p>Data analytics company loses on 22 out of 23 counts in lawsuit disputing how Swiss government rejected firm’s services</p><p>The US technology company Palantir has lost a legal challenge to force a Swiss independent magazine to publish its responses to articles about how the Swiss government rejected its services.</p><p>The data analytics company lost on 22 out of 23 counts of the suit. In a ruling on Friday, Zurich’s commercial court dismissed the majority of counterstatement requests filed by the company and its Swiss subsidiary finding that only a single passage in one article warranted a published response from the company.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2026/jun/13/palantir-loses-legal-challenge-to-force-swiss-magazine-to-publish-rejoinders\">Continue reading...</a>"
